  "review": {
    "base": "master",
    "branch": "m3/cell-extractor-primitive-counts-20261102",
    "title": "Array-back CellExtractor counts and CollatingIterator lookahead"
  },
  "review_statement": "## Problem and change\n\n`CellExtractor.from` retained TreeMap counter entries and allocated counter objects while collecting indexes. Replace that storage with primitive index/count/AVL/successor lanes, reusing the existing sparse Bloom algorithm. `CollatingIterator` now keeps fixed lookahead values in an Object array and uses the existing BitSet emptiness summary.\n\nPreserve signed index order, overflow, lazy/failed population, early return, comparator/child callback order, iterator state, and public APIs. Add exact-source differential tests and passive contract notes.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused Commons Maven suite on the final notice-complete sources: **376 tests; zero failures, errors, or skips**.\n- New coverage includes 400 seeded frequency scenarios, 32,768 monotonic indexes, and 180 collating callback traces.\n- Both production public descriptors are identical.\n- The same focused suite in the composed M3JDK Commons module also passed 376 tests on the final notice-complete sources.\n\n## Open merge gates\n\nExisting Checkstyle: 230 baseline findings, 232 candidate findings; only two new first-party test headers conflict with the inherited ASF fixed-header rule. RAT reports the same existing `CANDIDATES.tsv` failure in both trees and accepts all nine proposed files. R2 adds dated modification notices while preserving the original ASF headers. Focused Checkstyle was repeated with no new R2 findings; the full-tree style/RAT comparison above is the preserved R1 result. This PR does not assert that all remaining collection nodes have been converted.\n\n## Canonical execution\n\nCanonical recipe: `com.synexia.m3jdk.CollectionsContractRefinement20261017`, source revision **7af83c5ee4ad166d8cd45c6c33822debabd705ca**, review https://github.com/hsoliwal/com.synexia/pull/15427. Product bytes were emitted by actual qualified SDK Results and the second receive changed zero files. The canonical recipe and executable receiver remain in Synexia.\n",
